  "name": "Question 14",
  "problem": "Given that \n$|\\begin{aligned}3 & -2 \\\\ a & b+2\\end{aligned}|=8$,\nfind \n$|\\begin{aligned}3 & -2 \\\\ a+3 & b\\end{aligned}|.$",
  "worked_solution": "We \"factor out\" the given determinant from the determinant we would like to find:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}3 & -2 \\\\ a+3 & b\\end{aligned}| & =|\\begin{aligned}3 & -2 \\\\ a+3 & (b+2)-2\\end{aligned}|\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the linearity property of determinants, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}3 & -2 \\\\ a+3 & (b+2)-2\\end{aligned}| & ={{|\\begin{aligned}3 & -2 \\\\ a & b+2\\end{aligned}|}_{\u23df}}_{8}+|\\begin{aligned}3 & -2 \\\\ 3 & -2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =8+(-6+6) \\\\  & =8.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
